WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:07.859
Hi, welcome back to Tao Cidi.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.080
We're about to begin episode 9, which

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.320
I like to call "The Journey to the Center of the Sun."

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:20.900
We've already discussed some things big and powerful enough,

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:29.380
like a nuclear bomb used to clean ketchup off your shirt.

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:35.879
I'm not exaggerating, and I want you to think that way too. Imagine it's

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.410


00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.240
Independence Day in the United States, and I'm giving a speech on Independence Day.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:53.600
Usually, we go on picnics with our families, and it's midsummer.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:02.880
American kids eat hot dogs and hamburgers, and they put lots of ketchup on them. The
ketchup drips down here.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:13.200
Imagine cleaning it up, and Mom sends the shirt to the center of the sun

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.840
to clean up that tiny drop of ketchup, that red ketchup.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.380
I know this image sounds strange,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:31.020
but I want you to try to imagine it, just try to imagine it.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.060
I don't know what to compare it to.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.980
I don't know, just put some tiny thing into the center of the sun, okay?

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.120
So today we're going to visit the Sun Center.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:55.280
I'm happy to announce that we've reached the third and final part of the Path to

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.360
Enlightenment.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:04.700
Now we're about to delve into the activities of a Bodhisattva (the Bodhisattva path).

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:12.040
We're about to step into thinking and acting like a Bodhisattva, which

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:16.260
is the path of the superior being,
KYES BU CHEN PO,

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.700
meaning a person of great ability.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.280
Especially for those of you who have been following the Path to Enlightenment for nearly ten years,

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:33.860
you should be extremely happy that you've survived. I've also survived to the final part.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:37.580
We're talking about the final part, the last third.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.360
Now, the mathematicians among you should think about this: Geshe,

00:02:44.079 --> 00:02:46.529
you just said we still have 25% left.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:51.240
So why the last third?

00:02:51.240 --> 00:03:02.500
The answer is that the last two days of Pabongka Rinpoche's teachings on the Stages of the Path were too short.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:09.540
His explanations of meditation and the direct realization of emptiness—the

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:14.480
last two of the six perfections—were not very long.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.680
I don't know what happened; I mean, sometimes it's like a

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.820
sponsor comes to him and says, "We only have two days' worth of food left. Let's

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.860
summarize."

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:31.140
That's possible, or perhaps it's a mystical message from Tara.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:35.960
I don't know; maybe he had other appointments in other towns.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:50.480
But if you ask me, Pabongka Rinpoche shortened the last two parts
because Master Tsongkhapa had already covered this part in his

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.600
great treatise on the Stages of the Path.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:04:01.040
I think Master Tsongkhapa did an exceptionally good job; I can only see Pabongka Rinpoche saying,

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.540
"As you know, I have no reason to continue teaching this part,"

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:12.560
because Master Tsongkhapa had already taught it, and he taught it superbly.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.940
There are many, many stories about Master Tsongkhapa writing the last two parts.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.780
I'm happy that we've put them together to teach.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:29.260
We want to complete this Stages of the Path series with incredible teachings on meditation and emptiness.


00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:38.680
So that's why this part of the path for those with bodhicitta, and

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.440
this part for bodhisattvas,

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.020
doesn't have the length it should.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.640
Now we begin, we will read the Tibetan:

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.780
GSUM PA SKYES BU CHEN PO'I LAM GYI RIM
PAR BLO SBYANG BA LA.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:05:00.520
Let us cultivate our minds in the stages of the Bodhisattva path:

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.700
THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO SEMS BSKYED KHO NAR BSTAN PA PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.500
He said we will explain this Bodhisattva way of life.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.560
We will explain it in three different ways.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.440
First,

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.860
THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO.
If you want to enter the Bodhisattva path, there is only one way to do it, which is

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.620
by reaching a certain state of consciousness.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:29.660
If you want to attain enlightenment, if you want to have the opportunity to attain enlightenment,

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:36.260
if you want the opportunity to help the world, there is only one way—you need to have Bodhicitta.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:44.460
You must have the desire to help countless beings after attaining enlightenment.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.700
Now I want to talk about countless (concepts).

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:53.500
Bodhicitta is for countless beings.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:06:00.540
It does not refer to everyone in your city or your country, or everyone on this planet.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.920
Break it.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.800
If we want to launch a virus to the center of the sun, if we want to go to the center of the sun...

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:14.220
Break the idea that we're working for everyone on this planet. We're not like that. Break the

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:23.680
idea that we're trying to help all the fish, all the birds, and all the animals on the ground.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.840
We're not like that. That's

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:26.620
not what we mean.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.560
We encompass the entire universe. We're

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:39.300
deciding today that I'm going to help every life in the universe,

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.540
every tiny virus, every

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.360
bacterium,

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.300
every whale,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.640
every person in the universe.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:58.980
Go outside at night, in Santoro, or outside of Santoro, preferably Rim Rock.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:03.340
Look at the stars and let your imagination run wild.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:20.640
First,
you can't practice the Bodhisattva way of life (the Bodhisattva path)

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.709
if you don't extend your consciousness to that goal. If you really experience it, (of course) it takes some practice.

00:07:28.709 --> 00:07:30.850


00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:41.480
If you really send out your consciousness, if you can really attain Bodhicitta, then what you're doing in this world is nothing. It doesn't matter.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.780


00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:51.380
Helping everyone in this world is nothing, it's very simple.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:59.640
PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA means, I want to tell you the benefits of thinking like that, this is the first step.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.657
BYANG CHUB TU SEMS BSKYED PA'I TSUL is the second step.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:06.560
How do you achieve this breakthrough, a breakthrough of consciousness?

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:11.180
How do you view the entire universe and all life within it?

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:15.800
And then, is it possible to feel love for them?  Is

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.760
this possible?  This is the second step. The

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.560
third step, SEMS BSKYED NAS SPYOD PA LA SLOB TSUL LO.

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:27.080
We need to learn how to act like a Bodhisattva.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:34.900
Once you have the desire to become a Bodhisattva, then what should I actually do?

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:41.300
If I want to live like a Bodhisattva, how should I spend my day?  What

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.260
should I do?

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.600
What will my schedule look like?

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.200
OK  This is the first part.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:58.860
DANG PO NI,
DE LTAR SKYES BU CHUNG 'BRING GI SKABS SU NGES 'BYUNG GI BSAM PAS KUN NAS BSLANGS.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:08.340
Now that we have learned about the stages of practice for those on the lower and middle paths,

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:13.960
you should at least have this feeling:

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:17.100
This life is indeed painful, indeed full of troubles.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:20.580
Viruses make the pain more pronounced,

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.020
but in reality, it has always been like that. There has

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.940
always been a virus called death. The

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.280
current virus is newer and smaller,

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:33.340
but at least now we all think about it.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.220
LHAG PA'I BSLAB PA GSUM LA 'BAD PAS.

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:42.479
We should strive to cultivate the three trainings:

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.580
treat others kindly,

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.720
spend time meditating,

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:52.980
and try to understand that things do not come from themselves.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:59.540
'BAD PAS RANG GCIG PUS
THAR BA'I GO 'PHANG
THOB TZAM DANG 'KHOR BA
LAS LDOG TZAM 'BYUNG.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.960
You can attain Nirvana.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:06.980
You can also escape the cycle of life.

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:11.500
If you practice these attitudes, it is possible.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:14.000
We have already taught you, we have finished teaching that part of

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.000
DE TZAM GYIS MI CHOG,

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:18.347
but I don't want you to stop there.

00:10:18.347 --> 00:10:20.880
I don't want you to stop here. I want you to have

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.040
more important things to do, much

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:30.980
more important things to do. Don't stop there.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.680
SPANG BYA THAMS CAD MA SPANGS.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:39.500
If you only stick to what I have taught you so far, you

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:43.260
cannot purify your heart,

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.560
remove all impurities.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:50.240
THOB BYA YON TAN
THAMS CAD KYANG YONGS SU MA RDZOGS PAS.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.560
You will not reach

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.120
all the highest spiritual qualities you can achieve.

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:56.680
MA RDZOGS PAS. Therefore,

00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:02.480
RANG DON DANG,
GZHAN DON YANG NYI TSE BA LAS MI 'BYUNG

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:08.320
NYI TSE BA. This is a very discouraging word, a

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.600
very sad word.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:16.340
It says that you can work hard on the path of practice I have taught you so far.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.480
You can do all the meditations I have taught you,

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:25.120
but the number of good deeds you can do for yourself and others is

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:29.040
only a very small part of the good deeds you should do.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:34.900
NYI TSE BA means that it is only a very small part of what you should do.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:43.520
By the way, that word is most often used in Tibetan to mean hell on earth.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:45.900
It's strange that

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:49.580
there's a great hell that one person can go to,

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:56.840
but I always think of someone who gets into a car accident, the car explodes, and they are trapped in the fire.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:02.945
In the scriptures, this is called NYI TSI BA'I DMYAL BA,

00:12:02.945 --> 00:12:08.220
a small piece of hell on this airplane, on the airplane of "reality".

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:13.080
So the word NYI TSI BA means a very small piece.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:17.780
Here he says, do you want to help yourself and also want to help others?

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:22.420
For the past 10 years, all I've taught you is NYI TSI BA.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:30.160
That's only a tiny part of what you can do. Now we're going to start doing the real thing,

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:35.880
Geshe-la. Why have we spent 10 years on this little thing called NYI TSI BA?

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.460
Why don't we just learn things at a higher level?

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:44.660
Because the smaller things are the stepping stones to help you reach the higher things.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:50.080
Unless you do the other two parts first, you won't reach the higher levels.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:55.093
Unless you practice all the stages in the path in the correct order,

00:12:55.093 --> 00:12:58.460
you will never get to the Bodhisattva stage.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:02.560
So you can't just say you don't want to.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:10.260
Part of entering the Bodhisattva path is mastering the Hinayana to help you get there.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.760
You never refuse to come from them (the first two paths).

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:21.140
MI 'BYUNG ZHING SLAR THEG CHEN
LA GZHI NAS 'JUG DGOS LA.

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:27.320
This is a Buddhist perspective.

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.320
As long as you are ready,

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:32.460
as long as you are ready,

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.300
you can jump directly into the Bodhisattva lifestyle (entering the Bodhisattva path).

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:42.080
Because if you are not, you have to go through it all again.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.749
So sooner or later you will get here. Maybe it will

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:49.700
take this lifetime, maybe it will be in the later years of this life.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:57.780
Sometimes people come to me and say, I'm planning to leave Buddhism temporarily.

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:01.960
I feel I need to rest.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:05.740
I have other things I must do now. I have

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:10.600
a big project at work, or I have something to deal with at home.

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:15.600
I need to rest.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:19.400
I remember telling a teacher in India

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.350
45 years ago,

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:31.960
I said I need to rest, and they looked at me and said, okay, but you will come back.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:36.120
You will come back because you have nowhere else to go.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:44.300
You will come back, you will return here because you need to return here.  Life will bring you back here,

00:14:45.029 --> 00:14:47.929
because that's what life is like.  You need the stages of the path.

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:52.901
Life will always bring you back to the stages of the path, unless you die.

00:14:52.901 --> 00:14:55.680
It will still bring you back (on the path) in the future.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:02.600
SLAR means you have to come back again.
SLAR THEG CHEN LA GZHI NAS

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:07.250
GZHI NAS means that since you have to come back, you will waste a lot of time.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:12.780
You might as well finish it now instead of coming back later.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:17.360
Here is the next picture.

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:24.060
This is a little thing I want to do with you in episode 9.

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:27.400
I call it "Journey to the Center of the Sun".

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.000
In this picture, I

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:41.220
tried to find a picture similar to the feeling of attaining bodhicitta.

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:42.520
This picture is a bit like

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:46.280
me, Seiji and Tim, we were saying it's a bit novel. It's like it was

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:50.680
painted in San Dona, Arizona. It

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:58.120
feels a bit novel. Let me say a few words, if you can attain bodhicitta,

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:00.870
it feels like

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:10.660
this picture is very close.  This picture is somewhat similar.  Can you show it (this picture)?  Just for a moment.

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:15.700
This picture isn't crazy, nor is it anything hippie-ish.

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:22.540
When you attain bodhicitta, true bodhicitta, it feels a lot like this.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:28.040
Perhaps you want to copy this picture; we've already paid for it.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:32.680
You can use it at home, you can keep it at home,

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:38.320
you can save that picture, maybe even put it on your phone as a wallpaper.

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:43.660
It's very similar to the feeling of generating bodhicitta.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:49.280
So I want to take you on a fun little tour, about five minutes, and let's

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:55.540
review what it feels like

00:16:57.820 --> 00:17:03.100
when you truly generate bodhicitta for the first time.

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:12.480
We're not guessing what you call it, are we?  Partial Bodhicitta,

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:15.980
or trying to feel that you have Bodhicitta.  We're talking about real things. The day

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:24.120
you directly see emptiness, the day you directly experience Bodhicitta—

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:26.920
let's look at that day, because it's a stroke of luck.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.340
It's an atomic bomb.

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:36.660
If you keep trying, if you keep trying in this area,

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:41.200
to feel it (the feeling it brings you), if you keep listening to this part, it

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:43.551
will help destroy the virus.

00:17:43.551 --> 00:17:46.960
I believe it will help destroy the virus, like a nuclear weapon.

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:51.049
And the virus is like ketchup.
Let's begin.

00:17:53.040 --> 00:18:00.380
Let's try together for 5 minutes, imagining what it feels like to reach Bodhicitta. Let's
begin. Let's

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:06.320
take ten slow breaths together,

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:13.820
focusing on the exhale, a long exhale, don't pay attention to the inhale, your body will breathe (automatically).

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:52.540
Imagine you have directly seen emptiness.

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:57.450
You come out of the direct seeing of emptiness.

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:05.279
You return to what we call ordinary meditation, still not in this world.

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:10.529
You are in the depths of meditation, you are still sitting on the meditation mat.

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:14.190
Your eyes are closed.

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:25.900
Suddenly, the image of your mother appears in your consciousness, your mother. A

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:36.500
very, very perfect photograph of your mother, a living image, truly your mother.

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:40.400
Perhaps like the one you remember most clearly.

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:45.260
She is now just like that time. She is

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:51.140
gazing at you, she is gazing into your eyes.

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:58.700
Even if it feels like she is somewhere in front of your consciousness, she is looking into your eyes.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:10.260
With immense love and a strong sense of need, she desperately needs help.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.440
She's facing difficulties in some way,

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:23.120
like she jumped off the Titanic.
She looks at you with those eyes and says, "I need you, I need help."

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:42.560
Then you respond in your mind, "Don't worry, Mom, I'll take care of you.

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:50.100
I'll be strong enough to take care of you. Don't worry,

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:59.080
 
 
I will have the power to help you, and I will do it, I promise."

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:16.460
Then her image fades from your consciousness, and suddenly your father's picture appears. You

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:18.500
're looking at your father,

00:22:21.280 --> 00:22:31.260
and he has the same expression in his eyes—expectant and fearful.

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:37.400
He looks at you, as if saying, "Can you help me?"

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:42.500
Life is getting harder, life is tough now.

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:47.360
Then you say, "Dad, don't worry, I'm here!"

00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:49.820
I am studying the stages of the path.

00:22:50.200 --> 00:22:54.120
I am learning a lot about emptiness.

00:22:54.120 --> 00:23:01.280
Actually, I know I will soon have the tools to help you,

00:23:01.280 --> 00:23:04.680
so don't worry, I'm here, I will take care of you. You don't have to be

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:09.540
afraid, you don't have to worry.

00:23:09.540 --> 00:23:13.100
I know what to do, I'm doing it.

00:23:13.980 --> 00:23:17.120
Everything will be alright, so don't worry.

00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:29.280
Then another close person in your life, your wife or husband, or one of your children,

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:32.100
their image appears in your consciousness,

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:35.140
their face.

00:23:37.620 --> 00:23:44.940
They are looking at you, as if saying, "Can you help me? This is bad, this is really bad."

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:50.940
The situation is fatal, there is no other hope.  Can you help me?

00:23:54.220 --> 00:24:02.140
Then you say, "I'll take care of it, I can do it.

00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:07.920
I'll be able to take care of you.

00:24:07.920 --> 00:24:10.026
You really don't need to worry.

00:24:10.026 --> 00:24:11.623
I know what happened.

00:24:11.623 --> 00:24:13.220
I know your situation.

00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:17.015
I know what life is like.

00:24:17.020 --> 00:24:24.500
I've figured it out. I'll take perfect care of you.

00:24:24.680 --> 00:24:28.640
You don't need to worry, you really don't need to worry.

00:24:28.660 --> 00:24:31.320
I'll take care of you."

00:24:37.420 --> 00:24:43.320
Then that face gradually disappears, and you can start going through the faces of everyone you know—

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:48.000
close people, dear family members

00:24:49.260 --> 00:24:51.260
, uncles, aunts

00:24:51.680 --> 00:24:53.680
, brothers, sisters

00:24:55.280 --> 00:24:57.280
, nephews, nieces.

00:24:59.300 --> 00:25:07.420
One by one, you bring them to your face and comfort them.

00:25:08.480 --> 00:25:12.920
You say, "I really will handle it. You don't need to worry about anything." That's how

00:25:19.120 --> 00:25:22.000
we finish with everyone we know,

00:25:22.780 --> 00:25:25.480
everyone we've ever met in our lives.

00:25:26.480 --> 00:25:33.840
Then you start with everyone you've never met, everyone in the world.

00:25:34.500 --> 00:25:36.500
Starting from your community, then moving to the

00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:45.820
city, the whole city. Not that you can cover everyone,

00:25:46.440 --> 00:25:49.400
but pick someone from here, pick someone from there, and take them to the

00:25:50.940 --> 00:25:56.580
coastline of the continent where you live.

00:25:57.640 --> 00:25:59.640
Cover everyone.

00:26:00.900 --> 00:26:02.900
Then continue deeper,

00:26:03.860 --> 00:26:05.860
to other continents. That's how

00:26:07.920 --> 00:26:13.480
we cover everyone in the world.

00:26:15.920 --> 00:26:18.400
Just sit here,

00:26:19.160 --> 00:26:23.820
and then you can start facing the animals in the world, the fish.

00:26:24.920 --> 00:26:34.380
I'm not talking about the species of animals.
I'm talking about helping every animal. Everyone is

00:26:36.500 --> 00:26:39.890
looking at you, everyone is expecting something.

00:26:39.890 --> 00:26:44.260
Each one harbors fear, and each one receives your personal assurance:

00:26:44.620 --> 00:26:46.620
"I'm here, I'll handle it."

00:26:48.770 --> 00:26:53.679
Imagine browsing through every creature, the tiny creatures of the ocean floor, the

00:26:56.150 --> 00:26:58.150
tiny creatures in your blood.

00:26:59.780 --> 00:27:01.780
Go and meet every creature,

00:27:03.100 --> 00:27:05.260
talk to them.

00:27:05.720 --> 00:27:13.720
When you have completed all the life in this world, we will begin the next world.

00:27:13.720 --> 00:27:16.980
I don't know where the next world is, I don't know if it's Alpha Centauri?

00:27:17.660 --> 00:27:21.640
Perhaps many light-years away

00:27:24.040 --> 00:27:30.960
, go there and begin the same meditation for everyone in that world.

00:27:34.060 --> 00:27:41.660
In this way, we encompass every world in the entire universe, the

00:27:42.000 --> 00:27:51.740
karma of encountering 7 billion people one by one,

00:27:52.840 --> 00:27:57.600
and trillions of other beings on a planet.

00:27:58.060 --> 00:28:04.640
Then, as many planets as possible, countless planets,

00:28:04.640 --> 00:28:06.640
encompassing every life there.

00:28:09.680 --> 00:28:11.680
This is bodhicitta.

00:28:12.020 --> 00:28:15.820
This is the direct experience of bodhicitta.

00:28:15.840 --> 00:28:24.340
So please (try it), get this feeling in this episode.

00:28:26.140 --> 00:28:31.260
You don't have to worry about yourself, you don't have to worry about your family,

00:28:31.880 --> 00:28:35.080
you really don't have to worry about your country,

00:28:35.780 --> 00:28:40.740
you don't have to worry about the world covered by the virus. These are all small things.

00:28:41.720 --> 00:28:47.680
Of course, we will take care of them too.  The project we're working on is much larger.

00:28:49.460 --> 00:28:54.820
We're helping billions of lives throughout the universe,

00:28:55.920 --> 00:28:58.380


00:28:59.400 --> 00:29:03.560
billions of animals and other creatures.

00:29:05.140 --> 00:29:10.680
We truly have that ability, you truly have that ability, and I pray that you reach that state in this lifetime.

00:29:11.240 --> 00:29:14.760
I pray that you open it in this lifetime.

00:29:14.760 --> 00:29:28.840
Your consciousness already has the ability to touch every life
and promise them that you will care for them.

00:29:32.500 --> 00:29:36.700
The purpose of this path, the purpose of this retreat, is like

00:29:37.420 --> 00:29:40.160
traveling to the center of the sun.

00:29:40.600 --> 00:29:43.000
Think of every life,

00:29:43.360 --> 00:29:46.860
countless lives in the infinite universe,

00:29:48.320 --> 00:29:49.960
meeting one after another,

00:29:49.960 --> 00:29:51.420
making promises one after another.

00:29:52.220 --> 00:29:58.360
This is what happens when you first directly experience Bodhicitta. It

00:29:58.360 --> 00:29:59.980
really happens. This is how it

00:30:00.060 --> 00:30:01.843
feels.

00:30:01.843 --> 00:30:05.340
If you continue to imagine, it will help happen.

00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:07.020
Really. So it's up to

00:30:07.020 --> 00:30:10.759
you

00:30:11.340 --> 00:30:14.660
if you want it to come true. If you really want to become a true Bodhisattva,

00:30:15.680 --> 00:30:22.220
then
practice this visualization once or twice a day.

00:30:22.980 --> 00:30:28.140
Just a few minutes of your time, use your imagination to imagine it, okay?

00:30:29.159 --> 00:30:32.989
This helps it happen, and you will achieve Bodhicitta.

00:30:35.060 --> 00:30:43.120
Things like viruses are not important to a Bodhisattva.

00:30:43.120 --> 00:30:45.816
They are very, very small things.

00:30:45.820 --> 00:30:47.240
Earning money,

00:30:47.820 --> 00:30:49.360
making a living, supporting

00:30:49.600 --> 00:30:50.940
a family,

00:30:51.600 --> 00:30:53.600
finding shelter—

00:30:54.060 --> 00:30:58.660
these are incredibly small things; they are nothing.

00:31:00.240 --> 00:31:03.680
Your consciousness, your mind, is like the center of the sun.

00:31:05.180 --> 00:31:15.120
A few cookies or drops of Coca-Cola at the center of the sun are completely insignificant.

00:31:16.380 --> 00:31:18.040
They are not important.

00:31:18.560 --> 00:31:20.220
Do bigger things. Everything

00:31:21.440 --> 00:31:23.662
else becomes smaller.

00:31:23.662 --> 00:31:26.920
Everything else becomes comfortable and easy.

00:31:27.820 --> 00:31:29.820
This is Bodhicitta.

00:31:40.500 --> 00:31:43.220
See you next time.

00:31:43.220 --> 00:31:44.480
Episode 10.

